Determinism and privacy rules:
- Deterministic rules first. LLM is optional only for explanations/repairs in gray zones; never changes final thresholds.
- Read-only access to MR8; never write. Export new locations via CSV.
- No external logging of raw PII. Use src/utils/redact.ts. Mask ZIP to 5 digits and hash street lines in logs.
- Gracefully degrade when optional deps (libpostal, Tesseract, DB drivers) are unavailable. Tests must still pass.

Development rules:
- Core logic lives in src/. Both CLI and Next.js UI reuse the same modules.
- Keep TypeScript strict. Use Zod for runtime validation on external inputs.
- Keep thresholds and scoring in src/match/scorers.ts as exported constants.

Deterministic-first policy
- Prefer deterministic rules (phonetic/fuzzy/geo) before LLM.
- LLM is used only to repair/explain ambiguous cases; never to change match decisions.

Data handling
- Read-only access to MR8. No writes.
- Export NEW records to CSV only.
- Never log full PII; use `src/utils/redact.ts` helpers for masking/hashing.

Testing/CI
- No hard dependency on libpostal or tesseract in tests; degrade gracefully.



